      "side": 1,
      "message": "On Linux this subscribes to changes in NetworkManager’s full  active-connections  list, not changes to the primary/default-route connection. A secondary connection can therefore initiate call recovery unnecessarily, while a route change with the same active connections is not guaranteed to initiate it. Also,  QTimer::singleShot(500, ...)  queues one callback per notification rather than debouncing them; repeated callbacks force new recovery attempts",
